{"name":"Crystal Blue","hex":"#68a0b0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crystal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A solid composed of an array of atoms or molecules possessing long-range order and arranged in a pattern which is periodic in three dimensions.","A piece of glimmering, shining mineral resembling ice or glass."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of crystal.","Very clear; coherent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crystal"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crystal violet","blocks":[{"text":"Crystal violet or gentian violet, also known as methyl violet 10B or hexamethyl pararosaniline chloride, is a triarylmethane dye used as a histological stain and in Gram's method of classifying bacteria. Crystal violet has antibacterial, antifungal, and anthelmintic (vermicide) properties and was formerly important as a topical antiseptic. The medical use of the dye has been largely superseded by more modern drugs, although it is still listed by the World Health Organization."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Kristallviolett.svg/330px-Kristallviolett.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crystal_violet"},{"title":"Crystal","blocks":[{"text":"A crystal or crystalline solid is a solid material whose constituents are arranged in a highly ordered microscopic structure, forming a crystal lattice that extends in all directions. In addition, macroscopic single crystals are usually identifiable by their geometrical shape, consisting of flat faces with specific, characteristic orientations. The scientific study of crystals and crystal formation is known as crystallography. The process of crystal formation via mechanisms of crystal growth is called crystallization or solidification."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Quartz_28.jpg/330px-Quartz_28.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crystal"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Methyl_violet_10B_3D_ball.png/500px-Methyl_violet_10B_3D_ball.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Methyl_violet_10B_3D_ball.png/1280px-Methyl_violet_10B_3D_ball.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Methyl_violet_10B_3D_ball.png/500px-Methyl_violet_10B_3D_ball.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMethyl_violet_10B_3D_ball.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Sample_of_Crystal_Violet.jpg/500px-Sample_of_Crystal_Violet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Sample_of_Crystal_Violet.jpg/1280px-Sample_of_Crystal_Violet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Sample_of_Crystal_Violet.jpg/500px-Sample_of_Crystal_Violet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASample_of_Crystal_Violet.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Crystal_Violet_in_aqueous_solution.jpg/500px-Crystal_Violet_in_aqueous_solution.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Crystal_Violet_in_aqueous_solution.jpg/1280px-Crystal_Violet_in_aqueous_solution.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Crystal_Violet_in_aqueous_solution.jpg/500px-Crystal_Violet_in_aqueous_solution.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrystal_Violet_in_aqueous_solution.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Ditto_machine_copies_of_tests.jpg/500px-Ditto_machine_copies_of_tests.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Ditto_machine_copies_of_tests.jpg/1280px-Ditto_machine_copies_of_tests.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"